Capture the --cc-no-farble escape hatch that was live in the build tree but in no patch.

Every farbling entry point is gated on --fingerprint being present. This adds a second
condition so a run can keep the full persona (UA/screen/GPU/TLS/metadata) while turning
the per-eTLD+1 canvas/WebGL/audio/DOM perturbation OFF, without dropping --fingerprint.

That is a strictly different axis from --disable-fingerprint-noise, which the SDK already
exposes; the two overlap and should probably be reconciled. Captured here as-is because
this code is compiled into the shipped r10 binary and existed only in the working tree --
a tree reset would have silently lost it. Behaviour is unchanged: with the switch absent
(every shipped default and every SDK call path) each guard evaluates exactly as before.

NOTE: the switch is a raw string literal rather than a declared constant in
ungoogled_switches.h, unlike every other clearcote switch. Left as-found; promoting it is
a follow-up, not a capture.

